[513.54, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BPrefill is mostly spent in th\u001b[33G weight matmuls (about 84%, only ~450\u001b[71GGFLOP/s at M\u224876), with SwiGLU'\u001b[102G scalar expf\u001b[115Gtaking\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B9%. I'll bench\u001b[18Gark sgemm layouts for M\u224876\u001b[45Ga\u001b[47Gd M=512 to see wh\u001b[65Gther the block layout\u001b[87Gis costing\u001b[98Gprefill time.\r\u001b[3C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102man \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m she\u001b[13Gl command\u001b[23G \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BAt M=76, the b\u001b[18Gocked layout get\u001b[35G about 570 GFLOP/s in sgemm, n\u001b[66Garly the sam\u001b[79G as the original 586\u001b[104Gprefi\u001b[110Gl i\u001b[115G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bunaffected. I'm splitting W1/W3 and Q/K/V into s\u001b[52Gparate blocked\u001b[67Gmatrices\u001b[76Gnext,\u001b[82Gthen\u001b[87Glooking\u001b[95Gat\u001b[98Gload\u001b[103Gtime.\r\u001b[3C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m fi\u001b[13Ge, ran \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m shell commands \r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[39mGenerat\u001b[11Gon fell to 110\u2013116 tok/s,\u001b[37Ga\u001b[39Gd the classifier \u001b[57Glso slowed about\u001b[74G9%\u001b[77Gdespite no cod\u001b[92G change, so this looks\u001b[115Glike\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmachi\u001b[9Ge noise. I'm re-running the\u001b[37Gba\u001b[40Gdwidth probe to\u001b[56Gconfirm\u001b[65G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[4BBlock sizes "]
[513.542, "320\u2013384 have been the only\u001b[42Gconsi\u001b[48Gtently fast band, and all my block\u001b[84Gfall there\u001b[103Grunning\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Balternating binaries over sev\u001b[34Gal runs and comparing\u001b[56Gmedians. I'm\u001b[69Galso making BLOCK_MAX a\u001b[93Gbuild-time option for that.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m Decode holds at about 126\u001b[29Gtok/s\u001b[35Gacross\u001b[42Gwidths\u001b[49G256\u001b[53Gto\u001b[56G448,\u001b[61Gbut\u001b[65Gwidth\u001b[71G256\u001b[75Gprefills\u001b[84G17%\u001b[88Gfaster,\u001b[96Gso\u001b[99GI'm\u001b[103Gmaking\u001b[110Git\u001b[113Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdefault. Next I'll test whether transposing\u001b[47Gdirectly\u001b[56Gfrom\u001b[61Gan\u001b[64Gmmap\u001b[69Gof\u001b[72Gthe\u001b[76Gcheckpoint\u001b[87Gbeats\u001b[93Gthe\u001b[97Gstaging\u001b[105Gcopy\u001b[110Gfor\u001b[114Gload\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Btime.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m shell commands \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mTransposing straight from the mmap cuts load from about 114 to 103 ms with no effect on anything\u001b[100Gelse,\u001b[106Gso\u001b[109GI'm\u001b[113Gkeeping\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bit. I'll also try \u001b[38;"]
