[1067.719, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[41C\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mthought for 7s)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[1067.789, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2736\u001b[28G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m5\u001b[30G0\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[1067.811, "\u001b[H\u001b[7G\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m153\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m    \u001b[17G       \u001b[25G        \u001b[34G      \u001b[41G      \u001b[48G   \u001b[52G       \u001b[60G        \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m5\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mv1 kept the row-major layout\u001b[41Gwith fused QKV\u001b[56Gand W1/W3 weights,\u001b[75Gand\u001b[79Gused\u001b[84G`sgemv`/`sgemm`\u001b[100GNoTrans.\u001b[109GIt\u001b[112Gpa\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mssed the same check\u001b[32G and ran\u001b[41Gat\u001b[44G\u224879\u001b[48Gtok/s\u001b[54Gdecode.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mGeneration on the supplied workloads is now about 1.6\u00d7 faster: 121\u2013132 tok/s, up from 79.5. The rebuilt binary passes\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bboth \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcheck.py\u001b[39m runs (default and 3 prompts \u00d7 64 tokens). The largest logit error is 2.6e-5, against a tolerance of\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B5e-4.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat profiling showed\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mDecode is entirely limited by reading the weights.\u001b[22m 97% of the time went to the"]
[1067.813, " weight matrix-vector products,\u001b[115Gwhich\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bread memory at only 33\u201337 GB/s. Plain memory reads on this M1 reach 63 GB/s. My v1 notes said 34 GB/s was the\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bhardware limit; that was wrong, and NOTES.md now says so.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mWeight layout was the cause.\u001b[22m Stored transposed, in contiguous blocks 256\u2013384 columns wide, \u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemv\u001b[39m reads the weights\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bat about 63 GB/s.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mSmaller costs:\u001b[22m SwiGLU was 9% of prompt processing (one scalar \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mexpf\u001b[39m per element). Long-context attention cost about\u001b[120G4\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bms per token.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mTokenizer:\u001b[22m the reference's merge loop took 1.6 s on a 900-word prompt.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChanges\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B1.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mWeights are stored transposed in 256-column blocks\u001b[22m, with one Accelerate call per block. Prompt processing loses\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bnothing from this layout.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mQ/K/V and W1/W3 are now separate matrices.\u001b[22m K and V are written directly into t"]
[1067.815, "he KV cache, and SwiGLU runs as\u001b[116Ga\u001b[118Gfew\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bwhole-buffer vDSP/vForce calls in the reference's order of operations.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mThe embedding table is read from the transposed classifier\u001b[22m, so the weights are only held in memory once.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B4.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mLoading transposes straight from an mmap\u001b[22m of the checkpoint, with no staging copy.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B5.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mAttention over a chunk of prompt tokens skips the masked-out region.\u001b[22m Everything the reference computes is still\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bcomputed.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B6.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mFrom 160 positions onwards, single-token attention handles all heads with two \u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemm\u001b[39m calls per layer.\u001b[107G\u001b[22mThis\u001b[112Gadds\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   multiplications by zero\u001b[30Gbut\u001b[34Gremoves\u001b[42Gnone\u001b[47Gof\u001b[50Gthe\u001b[54Greference's\u001b[66Gwork.\u001b[72GBelow\u001b[78G160\u001b[82Gthe\u001b[86Gold\u001b[90Gper-head\u001b[99Gpath\u001b[104Gis\u001b[107Gkept\u001b[112Gbecause\r\u001b[1B     it is faster there.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B7.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mThe tokenizer caches the merge candidate for each adjacent pair.\u001b[71G\u001b[22mIts\u001b[75Goutput\u001b"]
[1067.815, "[82Gis\u001b[85Gidentical\u001b[95Gto\u001b[98Gthe\u001b[102Greference\u001b[112Galgorithm\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   on 514 test texts, including the fixtures and random\u001b[59GUnicode.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[1067.947, "\u001b[H\u001b[9G\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m4\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mv1\u001b[15Gkept\u001b[20Gthe\u001b[24Grow-major\u001b[34Glayout\u001b[41Gwith\u001b[46Gfused\u001b[52GQKV\u001b[56Gand\u001b[60GW1/W3\u001b[66Gweights,\u001b[75Gand\u001b[79Gused\u001b[84G`sgemv`/`sgemm`\u001b[100GNoTrans.\u001b[109GIt\u001b[112Gpa\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mssed the same checks and ran\u001b[41Gat \u224879 tok/s deco\u001b[59Ge.    \u001b[66G        \u001b[75G   \u001b[79G    \u001b[84G               \u001b[100G        \u001b[109G  \u001b[112G  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mGeneration\u001b[14Gon\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Gsupplied\u001b[30Gworkloads\u001b[40Gis\u001b[43Gnow\u001b[47Gabout\u001b[53G1.6\u00d7\u001b[58Gfaster:\u001b[66G121\u2013132\u001b[74Gtok/s,\u001b[81Gup\u001b[84Gfrom\u001b[89G79.5.\u001b[95GThe\u001b[99Grebuilt\u001b[107Gbinary\u001b[114Gpasses\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gboth \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcheck.py\u001b[17G\u001b[39mruns (default and 3 prompts \u00d7\u001b[47G64 tokens). The largest logit error is 2.6e-5, against a tolerance\u001b[114Gof\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B5e-4.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat profiling showed\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m- \u001b[1mDecode \u001b[13Gs entirely limited "]
[1067.949, "by reading the weights.\u001b[56G\u001b[22m97%\u001b[60Gof\u001b[63Gthe\u001b[67Gtime\u001b[72Gwent\u001b[77Gto\u001b[80Gthe\u001b[84Gweight\u001b[91Gmatrix-vector\u001b[105Gproducts,\u001b[115Gwhich\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gread memory at only 33\u201337 GB/s. Plain memory reads\u001b[56Gon this M1\u001b[67Greach 63 GB/s. My v1 notes said 34 GB/s was \u001b[112Ghe\u001b[115G\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bhar\u001b[9Gware limi\u001b[19G; that was wrong,\u001b[37Gand NOTES.md\u001b[50Gnow \u001b[55Gays\u001b[59Gso.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mWeight layout was the cause.\u001b[22m Store\u001b[41Gtransposed, in contiguous\u001b[67Gblocks\u001b[74G256\u2013384\u001b[82Gcolumns\u001b[90Gwide,\u001b[96G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemv\u001b[102G\u001b[39mreads\u001b[108Gthe\u001b[112Gweights\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gat about 63 GB/s.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mSmaller costs:\u001b[22m SwiGLU\u001b[27Gwas\u001b[31G9%\u001b[34Gof\u001b[37Gprompt\u001b[44Gprocessing\u001b[55G(one\u001b[60Gscalar\u001b[67G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mexpf\u001b[72G\u001b[39mper\u001b[76Gelement).\u001b[86GLong-context\u001b[99Gattention\u001b[109Gcost\u001b[114Gabout\u001b[120G4\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gms per token.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mTokenizer:\u001b[22m the\u001b[20Greference's\u001b[32Gmerge\u001b[38Gloop\u001b[43Gtook\u001b[48G1.6\u001b[52Gs\u001b[54Gon\u001b[57Ga\u001b[59G900-word\u001b[68Gprompt.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1"]
[1067.951, "mChanges\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m1. \u001b[1mWeights are stored transposed in 256-column blocks\u001b[22m,\u001b[58Gwith\u001b[63Gone\u001b[67GAccelerate\u001b[78Gcall\u001b[83Gper\u001b[87Gblock.\u001b[94GPrompt\u001b[101Gprocessing\u001b[112Gloses\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gnothing from this layout.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mQ/K/V and W1/W3 are now separate matrices.\u001b[49G\u001b[22mK\u001b[51Gand\u001b[55GV\u001b[57Gare\u001b[61Gwritten\u001b[69Gdirectly\u001b[78Ginto\u001b[83Gthe\u001b[87GKV\u001b[90Gcache,\u001b[97Gand\u001b[101GSwiGLU\u001b[108Gruns\u001b[113Gas\u001b[116Ga\u001b[118Gfew\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gwhole-buffer vDSP/vForce calls in the reference's ord\u001b[60Gr of operations.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mThe embedding table is read from the transposed classifier\u001b[22m, so the weights\u001b[81Gare\u001b[85Gonly\u001b[90Gheld\u001b[95Gin\u001b[98Gmemory\u001b[105Gonce.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B4\u001b[6G\u001b[1mLoading tra\u001b[18Gsposes straight\u001b[39Gan mmap\u001b[22m of the checkpoint\u001b[66Gwith no staging copy.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B5\u001b[6G\u001b[1mAttention over a chunk of prompt\u001b[39Gtokens skips the masked-out region.\u001b[22m Everything the\u001b[90Greference\u001b[100Gcomputes\u001b[109Gis\u001b[112Gstill\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gcomputed.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B6.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mFrom 160 positions onwards, s"]
[1067.952, "ingle-token attention handles all heads with two \u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemm\u001b[39m calls per layer.\u001b[107G\u001b[22mThis\u001b[112Gadds\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gmultiplications by zero but removes none of the reference's work. Below 160 the old per-head path is\u001b[107Gkept\u001b[112Gbecause\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bit is faster there.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B7.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mThe tokenizer caches the merge candidate for each adjacent pair.\u001b[71G\u001b[22mIts\u001b[75Goutput\u001b[82Gis\u001b[85Gidentical\u001b[95Gto\u001b[98Gthe\u001b[102Greference\u001b[112Galgorithm\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gon 514 test texts, including the fixtures and random Unicode.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mResults (medians of alternating runs)\u001b[22m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
